## SUMMARY

<span lang="ja">本書は、Textus/CNCFにおけるイミュータブルインフラストラクチャの目的、全体構造、状態管理、ライフサイクルおよび運用条件を説明します。第1・2章で目的と用語、第3・4章で構造と状態、第5章で交換時の動作を扱います。第6・7章ではセキュリティと運用条件を整理し、第8章で実装・検証状況、第9章で関連資料を示します。本文の設計記述と、採用版で実装・検証された範囲は区別します。</span><span lang="en">This guide describes the purpose, overall architecture, state management, lifecycle and operating conditions of immutable infrastructure in Textus/CNCF. Chapters 1 and 2 cover purpose and terminology; Chapters 3 and 4 cover architecture and state; Chapter 5 covers replacement behavior. Chapters 6 and 7 cover security and operating conditions, Chapter 8 records implementation and qualification status, and Chapter 9 lists related sources. Architectural descriptions are distinct from capabilities implemented and qualified in a selected version.</span>

<span lang="ja">本書は設計と運用モデルを説明する技術文書です。特定環境の操作コマンドや個別案件の作業手順は対象外です。設計上の構成、実装計画、採用版で確認された挙動を区別し、具体的な契約と検証結果は原典を参照します。</span><span lang="en">This technical guide describes the architecture and operating model. Commands for a particular environment and project-specific runbooks are outside its scope. Architectural structure, implementation plans and behavior qualified in a selected version are distinguished; source documents own concrete contracts and qualification results.</span>

# Purpose and Scope｜目的と対象範囲

<span lang="ja">イミュータブルインフラストラクチャは、変更を成果物と配備構成に反映し、それらから生成した新しい実行環境で既存の実行環境を置き換える運用方式です。稼働中の環境への直接変更を通常の更新方法とせず、交換する単位と、その生成に必要な入力を定めます。業務データの更新は実行環境の交換とは別に扱います。</span><span lang="en">Immutable infrastructure is an operating model in which changes are recorded in artifacts and deployment configuration, and a newly constructed environment replaces an existing environment. Routine updates use replacement rather than direct modification of a running environment. The replacement unit and its construction inputs are defined explicitly. Business-data updates are separate from runtime replacement.</span>

<span lang="ja">目的は、実行環境の構成を識別できること、同じ入力から環境を再構築できること、および更新を管理された交換単位で扱えることです。定期交換は、同じ環境を使用する期間を管理する運用に当たります。障害後の復旧だけでなく、通常運転中の部品更新、構成変更、環境の寿命管理を対象にします。再起動だけを繰り返す場合には、成果物と構成からの再構築や状態の分離は確認できません。</span><span lang="en">The objectives are identifiable runtime configuration, reconstruction from the same inputs and updates through controlled replacement units. Scheduled replacement manages the period for which an environment is used. The scope includes component updates, configuration changes and runtime lifetime management during ordinary service, as well as recovery after failure. Repeated restarts alone do not demonstrate reconstruction from artifacts and configuration or separation of state.</span>

<span lang="ja">本書では、交換可能性を成立させる設計条件と、その維持を求める枠組みを、設計上のハーネスとして位置付けます。交換・配備の単位について、責任のまとまり、単位間の依存、状態の所有、公開インターフェースと互換性を明示します。疎結合・高凝集などの特性を、依存してよい相手や、単位の内外で完結させる責任といった具体的な境界に落とし込みます。さらに、永続状態と一時状態の分離、構成・依存関係、起動・終了、受付済み処理の完了や回復の条件を定義します。これらは交換手順の外側にある設計上の成立条件です。</span><span lang="en">This guide describes a design harness as the framework that defines and maintains the architectural conditions needed for replaceability. For each replacement/deployment unit, the design identifies cohesive responsibilities, inter-unit dependencies, state ownership, public interfaces and compatibility. Properties such as loose coupling and high cohesion are expressed through concrete boundaries: permitted dependencies and responsibilities owned inside or outside a unit. The design also defines durable/transient state separation, configuration/dependencies, startup/shutdown and admitted-work completion/recovery conditions. These are architectural preconditions for the replacement procedure.</span>

<span lang="ja">CNCFでは、交換を支える基盤機構と、その上で動作するコンポーネントの実装契約を組み合わせて、このハーネスを利用します。基盤が状態管理、更新の確定、実行ライフサイクルなどの共通機構を担当し、コンポーネントはその契約に沿って業務処理を実装します。基盤の交換機構と、それを妨げないコンポーネント実装の両方が必要です。交換可能性への適合を継続して確認することにより、責任分離、明示的な依存関係、検証可能性および交換可能性を、コンポーネントの実装条件として維持します。</span><span lang="en">In CNCF, the harness combines platform mechanisms supporting replacement with implementation contracts for hosted components. The platform owns shared state-management, update-commit and execution-lifecycle mechanisms; components implement business behavior under those contracts. Both platform replacement mechanisms and compatible component implementations are required. Continuing replaceability checks maintain responsibility separation, explicit dependencies, testability and replaceability as component implementation conditions.</span>

<span lang="ja">CI/CDでも、継続的に検証・配備できる単位、再現可能な成果物と構成、および検証対象の依存関係を定義し、その条件を変更後も維持する必要があります。イミュータブル運用では、実行環境を再構築・交換できる条件も維持対象になります。採用した交換・配備方式がこれらの条件に依存するため、条件を満たさない変更は、検証や配備・交換の経路で検出・是正する対象です。特性を文書に掲げるだけでなく、実際の試験と配備・交換の結果で、守られていることを確認します。この継続的な制約と確認が、アーキテクチャの特性を維持するハーネスとして機能します。設計全体の正しさや、選択した検証項目の十分性を自動的に保証するものではありません。</span><span lang="en">CI/CD likewise requires defined units for continuous verification/deployment, reproducible artifacts/configuration and explicit dependencies under verification; changes must preserve those conditions. Immutable operation additionally requires maintained conditions for runtime reconstruction/replacement. Because the selected deployment/replacement method depends on these conditions, violations are subjects for detection and correction through its verification and deployment/replacement paths. Actual tests and deployment/replacement results establish whether the properties are maintained, rather than a written declaration alone. These ongoing constraints and checks function as a harness for architectural properties. They do not automatically guarantee whole-design correctness or the sufficiency of the selected checks.</span>

<span lang="ja">本書は、業務アプリケーションを動かすApplicationティアと、メモリ常駐を利用するDomainティアを対象にします。停止を許容する構成では単一環境を停止して再構築できます。交換中も業務を継続する構成では、別環境の準備、受付の切替え、データ同期、旧処理の完了管理が必要です。対応する故障の範囲と業務継続の水準は、HA構成として別に定めます。</span><span lang="en">The guide covers the Application tier serving business applications and the Domain tier using memory-resident execution. A deployment that permits downtime can stop and reconstruct a single environment. Continuing service during replacement requires preparation of another environment, admission transfer, data synchronization and completion management for old work. The supported failure boundary and continuity level are defined separately by the HA deployment.</span>

# Concepts and Applicability｜基本概念と適用条件

<span lang="ja">関連する概念の役割</span><span lang="en">Roles of Related Concepts</span>

| <span lang="ja">概念</span><span lang="en">Concept</span> | <span lang="ja">意味</span><span lang="en">Meaning</span> | <span lang="ja">それだけでは保証しないこと</span><span lang="en">Not Guaranteed Alone</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">Immutable</span><span lang="en">Immutable</span> | <span lang="ja">稼働中の環境を変更せず、新しい環境へ交換する</span><span lang="en">Replace an environment rather than changing it in place</span> | <span lang="ja">短命性、無停止、データの永続性</span><span lang="en">Short lifetime, uninterrupted service or data durability</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Ephemeral</span><span lang="en">Ephemeral</span> | <span lang="ja">寿命を短く管理し、実行環境を破棄できるようにする</span><span lang="en">Manage short lifetimes and disposable environments</span> | <span lang="ja">構成の再現性やデータ保全</span><span lang="en">Reproducible configuration or preserved data</span> |
| <span lang="ja">HA</span><span lang="en">HA</span> | <span lang="ja">定めた障害範囲と運用条件でサービス継続を支える</span><span lang="en">Support service continuity within defined failure and operating boundaries</span> | <span lang="ja">すべての障害への耐性やバックアップ</span><span lang="en">Tolerance of every failure or backups</span> |
| <span lang="ja">永続化</span><span lang="en">Persistence</span> | <span lang="ja">必要な業務状態を実行環境の寿命から分離する</span><span lang="en">Separate required business state from runtime lifetimes</span> | <span lang="ja">保存基盤自体の障害への無条件な耐性</span><span lang="en">Unconditional survival of storage failure</span> |
| <span lang="ja">定期交換</span><span lang="en">Scheduled replacement</span> | <span lang="ja">運用方針に従う間隔で実行環境を交換する</span><span lang="en">Replace runtime environments at policy-selected intervals</span> | <span lang="ja">交換中の継続性や障害時の引継ぎ</span><span lang="en">Continuity during replacement or takeover after failure</span> |

<span lang="ja">定期交換では同じ部品版を用いて実行環境を再構築し、部品更新では新しい版のCARを用います。交換間隔は運用方針です。いずれも実行環境を交換する操作であり、正本の業務データを過去の状態へ戻す操作ではありません。無停止運転、実行環境の短命性、データの永続性は、それぞれに必要な構成と条件で確認する性質です。</span><span lang="en">Scheduled replacement reconstructs an environment using the same component version; a component update uses a newer CAR version. Replacement cadence is an operating policy. Both replace an execution environment without rewinding authoritative business data. Uninterrupted operation, short runtime lifetimes and data durability each require their own configuration and qualification conditions.</span>

# Overall Architecture｜全体アーキテクチャ

<span lang="ja">以下は、Textus/CNCFで実行環境を交換するための設計上の構成です。成果物と構成、環境を生成する配備系、業務を処理する実行系、正本と常駐状態を扱うデータ系、受付権限と寿命を管理する制御系、および観測を区別します。これらは責任の区分であり、各区分を必ず独立した製品やホストに配置する意味ではありません。</span><span lang="en">The following is the intended Textus/CNCF structure for runtime replacement. It distinguishes artifacts/configuration, deployment, business execution, authoritative/resident data, admission/lifecycle control and observation. These are responsibility boundaries rather than a requirement for separate products or hosts.</span>

<span lang="ja">構成要素と接続関係</span><span lang="en">Elements and Connections</span>

| <span lang="ja">構成要素</span><span lang="en">Element</span> | <span lang="ja">担当する状態・処理</span><span lang="en">State or Processing Responsibility</span> | <span lang="ja">主な接続関係</span><span lang="en">Principal Connections</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">成果物・構成</span><span lang="en">Artifacts and configuration</span> | <span lang="ja">CAR、実行環境の定義、配備設定を識別する</span><span lang="en">Identify CARs, runtime definitions and deployment settings</span> | <span lang="ja">配備系へ新環境の生成入力を渡す</span><span lang="en">Supply construction inputs to deployment</span> |
| <span lang="ja">配備系</span><span lang="en">Deployment</span> | <span lang="ja">実行環境を生成・停止し、資源へ対応付ける</span><span lang="en">Create/stop environments and map them to resources</span> | <span lang="ja">成果物・構成を読み、制御系の判断に従う</span><span lang="en">Consume artifacts/configuration and control decisions</span> |
| <span lang="ja">入口・受付経路</span><span lang="en">Entry and admission route</span> | <span lang="ja">業務APIを受け付け、対象の実行環境へ渡す</span><span lang="en">Accept business API requests and pass them to an environment</span> | <span lang="ja">権限と準備条件に対応した受付先を使う</span><span lang="en">Use destinations qualified by authority and readiness</span> |
| <span lang="ja">実行系</span><span lang="en">Execution</span> | <span lang="ja">ApplicationとDomain Subsystemの業務処理を実行する</span><span lang="en">Run Application and Domain Subsystem business processing</span> | <span lang="ja">受付経路、UnitOfWork、常駐状態と接続する</span><span lang="en">Connect admission, UnitOfWork and resident state</span> |
| <span lang="ja">正本・永続記録</span><span lang="en">Authoritative storage and durable records</span> | <span lang="ja">確定した業務状態と対応する継続記録を保持する</span><span lang="en">Retain committed business state and supported continuation records</span> | <span lang="ja">UnitOfWorkの更新と再構築・回復の参照先になる</span><span lang="en">Serve UnitOfWork commits and reconstruction/recovery reads</span> |
| <span lang="ja">常駐状態・同期系</span><span lang="en">Resident state and synchronization</span> | <span lang="ja">Entity、索引、Working Set、Viewなどを再構築・反映する</span><span lang="en">Reconstruct/update Entities, indexes, Working Sets and Views</span> | <span lang="ja">正本の初期状態と確定差分を用い、各環境へ反映する</span><span lang="en">Use authoritative baselines and committed deltas across environments</span> |
| <span lang="ja">制御系・調停基盤</span><span lang="en">Control and coordination</span> | <span lang="ja">受付権限、準備条件、保持・退役の条件を管理する</span><span lang="en">Manage admission authority, readiness, retention and retirement conditions</span> | <span lang="ja">調停基盤、実行系、配備系および入口と接続する</span><span lang="en">Connect coordination, execution, deployment and entry</span> |
| <span lang="ja">観測系</span><span lang="en">Observation</span> | <span lang="ja">実際の状態、処理結果と切替えの理由を記録する</span><span lang="en">Record actual state, work outcomes and transition reasons</span> | <span lang="ja">実行・同期・制御・配備の状態を運用者へ示す</span><span lang="en">Expose execution/synchronization/control/deployment state to operators</span> |

<span lang="ja">環境生成の経路では、配備系が対象版のCAR、実行環境の定義および配備構成を入力として、新しい実行環境を生成します。準備確認では、成果物・データの互換性、正本への接続および必要な常駐状態の構築状況を扱います。稼働中の環境は、新環境の生成元として手作業で変更を蓄積する場所ではなく、識別された版と構成で動作する交換対象です。</span><span lang="en">The construction path supplies deployment with a selected CAR version, runtime definition and deployment configuration to create a new environment. Readiness covers artifact/data compatibility, authoritative connectivity and construction of required resident state. A running environment is a replaceable instance of an identified version/configuration, rather than a place to accumulate manual changes as the source for its successor.</span>

<span lang="ja">業務要求の経路では、安定した入口から、受付権限と準備条件を満たす実行環境へ要求を渡します。Domainの更新はUnitOfWorkを通して正本へ確定し、その結果を常駐状態やRead Replicaへ反映する設計です。実行環境の交換と正本の業務データの更新は、別の経路として扱います。</span><span lang="en">The service path passes requests from a stable entry to an execution environment satisfying admission authority and readiness. Domain updates commit to authoritative storage through UnitOfWork, and their outcomes update resident state and Read Replicas in the design. Runtime replacement and authoritative business-data updates are separate paths.</span>

<span lang="ja">制御系は、調停基盤の権限と各環境の準備・同期・処理状態を用いて、受付変更、保持および退役の可否を判断します。配備系はその判断に対応して環境を生成・停止し、入口は受付先を変更します。観測系は版、役割、反映位置、完了待ちおよび失敗理由を記録します。新環境が起動したという情報だけでは、業務の受付や旧環境の停止は許可されません。</span><span lang="en">Control uses coordination authority and observed readiness, synchronization and work state to decide admission changes, retention and retirement. Deployment creates/stops environments according to those decisions, while the entry changes its destination. Observation records versions, roles, applied progress, draining work and failure reasons. Environment startup alone does not authorize business admission or retirement of an old environment.</span>

## Tier Structure and Responsibilities｜ティア構成と責任分担

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFの構造では、状態管理と実行ライフサイクルの共通機構を基盤側に置き、コンポーネントが利用する契約として定めます。アプリケーションは業務規則と更新・継続処理をその契約に沿って実装し、基盤は準備確認、受付変更、同期、旧処理の完了管理および退役を担当します。業務アプリケーションごとのA・B・C切替え実装を前提とせず、配備プロファイルと設定で交換を選択する構成です。採用版で提供される機構と、計画中の交換制御・検証項目は、第8章の実装状況と原典で区別します。</span><span lang="en">The Textus/CNCF structure places shared state-management and execution-lifecycle mechanisms in the platform and defines their component-facing contracts. Applications implement business rules and update/continuation behavior under those contracts; the platform owns readiness, admission changes, synchronization, completion management and retirement. Profiles and configuration select replacement without application-specific A/B/C transfer logic. Chapter 8 and the owning sources distinguish mechanisms available in a selected version from planned replacement control and qualification work.</span>

<span lang="ja">責任の分担</span><span lang="en">Responsibility Boundaries</span>

| <span lang="ja">担当</span><span lang="en">Owner</span> | <span lang="ja">役割</span><span lang="en">Responsibility</span> |
| --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">業務アプリケーション</span><span lang="en">Business application</span> | <span lang="ja">業務規則、操作の意味、更新の競合条件、継続・再実行可能な区切り</span><span lang="en">Business rules, operation meaning, concurrency conditions and supported continuation/retry boundaries</span> |
| <span lang="ja">CNCF Runtime</span><span lang="en">CNCF Runtime</span> | <span lang="ja">新規受付と旧処理の完了権限、準備状態、同期、切替えと退役の条件</span><span lang="en">New admission and scoped completion authority, readiness, synchronization, transfer and retirement conditions</span> |
| <span lang="ja">配備・調停・保存基盤</span><span lang="en">Deployment, coordination and storage infrastructure</span> | <span lang="ja">実行環境の生成・停止、選出とLease、実効的なFencing、正本の永続化</span><span lang="en">Runtime creation/stop, election and Lease, effective fencing and authoritative persistence</span> |
| <span lang="ja">運用担当者</span><span lang="en">Operator</span> | <span lang="ja">品質目標、障害範囲、交換間隔、保持、資源予算、異常時の判断</span><span lang="en">Quality targets, failure boundary, cadence, retention, resource budget and incident decisions</span> |

<span lang="ja">Applicationティアでは、適した処理にCloud Functionの実行環境の再利用・廃棄を用いる構成を想定します。Domainティアでは、メモリ常駐状態を準備した環境へ交代します。Primaryは新規更新を受け付ける役割、Read Replicaは許可された参照を提供する役割です。Standbyは昇格に必要な準備を満たす性質であり、参照可能であることとは別に判定します。これらは論理的な役割であり、物理ホストの台数を指定するものではありません。</span><span lang="en">The intended Application-tier structure uses Cloud Function environment reuse and disposal for suitable work. The Domain tier transfers service to an environment with prepared resident state. Primary is the role accepting new mutations; Read Replica is the role serving permitted reads. Standby denotes promotion readiness, assessed separately from read availability. These are logical roles rather than a prescribed physical host count.</span>

<span lang="ja">実装契約は、自動生成部分に加えて、アプリケーション固有の追加実装にも適用します。追加コードを人が書く場合もAIが生成する場合も、同じ条件です。具体的には、業務継続に必要な状態を特定プロセスのメモリや交換対象のローカルファイルだけに保持しないこと、更新を対応する正本・UnitOfWorkの確定経路へ接続すること、および処理の開始・終了・完了・再開を基盤の契約に合わせることが必要です。バックグラウンド処理や外部副作用も、寿命と完了・回復の責任を明示します。追加実装を含む実際の業務経路で交換・回復を確認することが、適合性の確認になります。生成方式や使用したAIモデルは、その確認を代替しません。</span><span lang="en">The implementation contracts apply to application-specific additions as well as generated code, with the same conditions for human-written and AI-generated additions. Continuity-critical state must not reside solely in process memory or local files belonging to the replaceable environment. Updates connect to the applicable authoritative/UnitOfWork commit path, and processing start, shutdown, completion and resumption follow platform contracts. Background work and external effects have explicit lifetime and completion/recovery ownership. Conformance is qualified through actual business paths including the additions, exercising replacement and recovery. The generation method or AI model used does not substitute for those checks.</span>

# State Management and Application Boundaries｜状態管理とアプリケーションの境界

<span lang="ja">CNCFのDomain Subsystemは、EntitySpace、Entity Realm、索引、Working SetやViewをメモリに保持し、繰り返しの取得・構築を減らす設計です。正本の業務状態とメモリ常駐状態の寿命は分けます。業務継続に必要な確定状態を特定プロセスのメモリだけに置かず、実行環境を交換した後に必要な常駐状態を再構築する構造を取ります。</span><span lang="en">CNCF Domain Subsystems are designed to retain EntitySpace, Entity Realms, indexes, Working Sets and Views in memory to reduce repeated retrieval and construction. Authoritative business state and resident memory have separate lifetimes. Committed state needed for continuity does not reside solely in one process; the required resident state is reconstructed after runtime replacement.</span>

<span lang="ja">更新はDomainの規則とUnitOfWorkを通して正本の保存先へ確定し、その結果に従ってメモリの状態を更新・無効化する設計です。業務上の確定成功は、採用する保存先の永続化契約を満たすことに対応します。メモリへの反映やReplicaへの通知は、保存先での確定とは別の状態です。実際の保全範囲は、保存先との接続と永続化・回復の確認結果に依存します。</span><span lang="en">The design commits updates to authoritative storage through Domain rules and UnitOfWork, then updates or invalidates resident state according to the outcome. Business commit success corresponds to the durability contract of the selected storage. Memory updates and Replica notifications are separate from authoritative commit. The actual preservation boundary depends on storage integration and observed durability and recovery behavior.</span>

<span lang="ja">交換時に区別する状態</span><span lang="en">State Categories During Replacement</span>

| <span lang="ja">状態</span><span lang="en">State</span> | <span lang="ja">扱い</span><span lang="en">Treatment</span> |
| --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">確定した業務データ・資料</span><span lang="en">Committed business data and materials</span> | <span lang="ja">実行環境と別に保持・保護し、交換後も引き継ぐ</span><span lang="en">Retain and protect independently of the runtime</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Entityの常駐状態・索引・キャッシュ</span><span lang="en">Resident Entities, indexes and caches</span> | <span lang="ja">正本と確定差分から必要な範囲を再構築する</span><span lang="en">Reconstruct the required scope from authoritative state and committed changes</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Job・Workflowの継続に必要な記録</span><span lang="en">Records needed to continue Jobs and Workflows</span> | <span lang="ja">対応する永続化済みの区切りと回復契約に従う</span><span lang="en">Use supported durable boundaries and recovery contracts</span> |
| <span lang="ja">実行中の一時状態・未確定の更新</span><span lang="en">Transient execution state and uncommitted updates</span> | <span lang="ja">計画交換では完了を待ち、クラッシュ時は実際の確定結果を照合する</span><span lang="en">Drain during planned replacement; reconcile actual outcomes after a crash</span> |

<span lang="ja">常駐状態の再構築では、正本の整合した初期状態を取得し、構築中に確定した更新へ追随します。必要な反映位置と参照条件を満たすことが利用開始の条件です。別機からのメモリコピーや通知の受信だけでは、必要な確定状態がすべて反映されたかは判定できません。</span><span lang="en">Reconstruction obtains a consistent authoritative baseline and catches up with updates committed during loading. Use begins when required applied progress and read conditions are satisfied. A memory copy from another runtime or receipt of notifications alone does not establish that all required committed state has been applied.</span>

<span lang="ja">計画交換では、有効な権限の下で受付済み処理の結果を確定させてから旧環境を退役させます。クラッシュでは途中の計算を失う場合があるため、確定済み、未確定、結果不明を保存先の記録と照合します。Job・Workflowの再開は、対応する永続化済みの区切りと回復契約に従います。任意のRunning処理の自動再実行は前提にしません。データ保全の範囲には、保存基盤の障害範囲、バックアップおよび復旧方針も含まれます。</span><span lang="en">Planned replacement retires an old environment after admitted work reaches a settled outcome under valid authority. A crash can lose intermediate computation, so committed, uncommitted and uncertain outcomes are reconciled with storage records. Job and Workflow resumption follows supported durable checkpoints and recovery contracts. Arbitrary Running work is not assumed to be replayable. Data preservation also depends on storage failure boundaries, backup and recovery policy.</span>

# Lifecycle and Operation｜ライフサイクルと運用

<span lang="ja">本章は、前章までの構成要素が交換時にどのように動作するかを説明します。通常の計画交換と、権限喪失・クラッシュ・侵害が疑われる場合の動作は、成立条件が異なります。以下は設計上の動作であり、採用版の提供範囲と確認状況は第8章に示します。</span><span lang="en">This chapter describes how the preceding elements participate in replacement. Planned replacement and handling of authority loss, crashes or suspected compromise have different preconditions. The behavior below describes the design; Chapter 8 records delivery and qualification status for the selected scope.</span>

<span lang="ja">以下の計画交換例では、Aが旧Primary、Bが受付を引き継ぐ環境、Cが新しく準備するRead Replicaです。A・B・Cは役割の変化を説明する名前であり、常時三台の物理ホストを使用する指定ではありません。</span><span lang="en">In the planned-replacement example, A is the former Primary, B takes over admission and C is the newly prepared Read Replica. A/B/C describe changing roles and do not specify three continuously running physical hosts.</span>

## Planned Replacement｜計画交換

<span lang="ja">計画交換の説明では、AをPrimary、BをRead Replica兼Standbyとします。Bが互換性、正本接続、同期および準備条件を満たした後、新規の参照・更新の受付をBへ移します。Aでは新規の独立した処理を停止し、切替え前に受け付けた更新と、その完了に必要な処理を、有効な限定権限の下で継続します。</span><span lang="en">The planned-replacement example uses A as Primary and B as a Read Replica qualified as Standby. New read/write admission moves to B after compatibility, authoritative connectivity, synchronization and readiness conditions are satisfied. A stops new independent work and completes updates admitted before transfer, including necessary completion work, under valid scoped authority.</span>

<span lang="ja">Bの新規受付後、代替Read Replica Cを生成して常駐状態を構築します。Aで遅れて確定した更新もB・Cへ反映し、切戻し候補として残るAも現在の確定状態へ追随します。同期基盤はA・Bの組だけでなく、複数Replica、構築中の環境および保持中の環境を扱う設計です。A・B・Cは役割の変化を説明する名前であり、常時三台の運用を定めるものではありません。</span><span lang="en">After B begins accepting new work, replacement Read Replica C is created and its resident state is constructed. Late commits from A reach B/C, and A catches up with current committed state while retained as a switch-back candidate. The synchronization design supports multiple Replicas and environments under construction or retention, rather than a dedicated A/B copy. A/B/C describe changing roles and do not prescribe three continuously running machines.</span>

<span lang="ja">交換段階の条件</span><span lang="en">Conditions by Replacement Stage</span>

| <span lang="ja">段階</span><span lang="en">Stage</span> | <span lang="ja">確認すること</span><span lang="en">Check</span> |
| --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">交換前</span><span lang="en">Before transfer</span> | <span lang="ja">成果物・データ互換性、準備状態、同期位置、利用可能な資源</span><span lang="en">Artifact/data compatibility, readiness, synchronization position and resources</span> |
| <span lang="ja">受付切替え</span><span lang="en">Admission transfer</span> | <span lang="ja">Bの新規受付権限と、Aの新規受付停止・限定された完了権限</span><span lang="en">B new-admission authority; A closed admission and scoped completion authority</span> |
| <span lang="ja">旧処理の完了</span><span lang="en">Old-work completion</span> | <span lang="ja">commit・abort・失敗・結果不明の実態。HTTP応答だけでは判定しない</span><span lang="en">Actual commit, abort, failure or uncertainty; not HTTP completion alone</span> |
| <span lang="ja">保持・観測</span><span lang="en">Retention and observation</span> | <span lang="ja">Cの準備、Aの同期、データ互換性と切戻し可能性</span><span lang="en">C readiness, A synchronization, data compatibility and switch-back eligibility</span> |
| <span lang="ja">退役</span><span lang="en">Retirement</span> | <span lang="ja">旧処理の結果確定、代替参照容量、保持・観測条件、未解決事項</span><span lang="en">Settled old work, replacement read capacity, retention/observation conditions and outstanding issues</span> |

<span lang="ja">Aの退役条件は、旧処理の結果確定、代替参照容量、必要な同期、および設定された保持・観測条件です。結果不明の更新、未準備のC、未完了の同期は退役を保留する理由になります。新Primaryの応答や保持時間の経過だけでは、これらの条件は満たされません。権限を失った環境や侵害が疑われる環境には、通常の完走・切戻し条件を適用しません。</span><span lang="en">A retires when old-work outcomes are settled, replacement read capacity is available, required synchronization is complete and configured retention/observation conditions hold. Uncertain updates, an unready C or incomplete synchronization defer retirement. A responsive new Primary or elapsed retention time alone does not satisfy these conditions. Authority loss or suspected compromise requires handling outside ordinary completion and switch-back conditions.</span>

## Scheduled Replacement, Updates and Switch-back｜定期交換・部品更新・切戻し

<span lang="ja">交換間隔は、脅威への対応、更新頻度、起動・ウォームアップの費用および業務時間帯に対応する運用設定です。日次交換は選択例であり、固定の標準値ではありません。スケジュール時刻は交換開始の契機です。受付済み更新の強制中断や、退役条件を省略する期限とは分けて扱います。</span><span lang="en">Replacement cadence is an operating setting related to threat response, update frequency, startup/warm-up cost and business service windows. Daily replacement is one option rather than a fixed default. A scheduled time triggers replacement; it is separate from forced interruption of admitted updates or omission of retirement conditions.</span>

<span lang="ja">部品更新は、新しいCARと構成による環境生成、互換性と利用経路の確認、受付変更および観測から成ります。配備の確定は、受付先の変更だけでなく、設定した観測条件を満たすことに対応します。定期交換と互換CARへの交換は、同じ交換機構を利用する設計です。</span><span lang="en">A component update comprises environment construction from a new CAR and configuration, compatibility and route checks, admission transfer and observation. Deployment acceptance depends on configured observation conditions as well as the admission change. Scheduled replacement and compatible CAR updates use the same replacement mechanism in the design.</span>

<span lang="ja">切戻しの対象は、現在の業務データと構成に互換性があり、必要な同期・準備を満たし、受付権限を取得できる保持環境です。切戻しでも現在の確定状態を利用します。データ互換性を壊す変更は通常の自動交換の対象から分け、計画したメンテナンス更新として扱います。</span><span lang="en">A switch-back candidate is a retained environment compatible with current business data and configuration, with required synchronization/readiness and valid admission authority. Switch-back continues from current committed state. Changes that break data compatibility are handled as planned maintenance updates rather than ordinary automatic replacement.</span>

## Exceptional and Failure Behavior｜例外・障害時の動作

<span lang="ja">例外状態と対応条件</span><span lang="en">Exceptional States and Handling Conditions</span>

| <span lang="ja">状況</span><span lang="en">Situation</span> | <span lang="ja">扱い</span><span lang="en">Treatment</span> |
| --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">交換先の準備不足</span><span lang="en">Replacement unready</span> | <span lang="ja">受付を移さず、準備できない理由を確認する</span><span lang="en">Do not transfer admission; examine why readiness failed</span> |
| <span lang="ja">旧処理の長期化</span><span lang="en">Prolonged old work</span> | <span lang="ja">実際の状態を観測し、継続・業務対応を判断する。予定時刻だけで打ち切らない</span><span lang="en">Observe actual state and choose continuation/business action; do not terminate solely on schedule</span> |
| <span lang="ja">クラッシュ・権限喪失</span><span lang="en">Crash or authority loss</span> | <span lang="ja">旧権限での更新を拒否し、正当な権限・Fencing・準備が揃った経路だけで引き継ぐ</span><span lang="en">Reject invalid-authority writes; take over only with valid ownership, fencing and readiness</span> |
| <span lang="ja">侵害の疑い</span><span lang="en">Suspected compromise</span> | <span lang="ja">隔離・失効と原因調査を優先し、疑わしい旧環境への切戻しを認めない</span><span lang="en">Prioritize isolation, revocation and investigation; refuse fallback to the suspected runtime</span> |
| <span lang="ja">正本の破損・利用不可</span><span lang="en">Authoritative state corrupt or unavailable</span> | <span lang="ja">実行環境の交換だけで解決したとせず、保存・復旧の手順へ接続する</span><span lang="en">Use storage/recovery procedures; runtime replacement alone does not resolve it</span> |

<span lang="ja">計画切替えは旧Primaryが協調動作できる場合の手順です。障害切替えでは、到達不能な旧機の更新をFencingで拒否し、正当な引継ぎ権限と準備を確認してから受付を開始します。途中の処理は実際の確定結果と照合します。ロードバランサーの変更や稼働確認は、権限の強制や結果照合とは別の機能です。</span><span lang="en">Planned Switchover assumes cooperation by the old Primary. Failover fences writes from an unreachable old environment and starts admission only after valid takeover authority and readiness are established. Interrupted work is reconciled with actual committed outcomes. Load-balancer changes and liveness checks are separate from authority enforcement and outcome reconciliation.</span>

<span lang="ja">自動障害切替えの未提供・未検証は、採用構成の制約として記録します。正当な更新権限または必要なデータを確認できない範囲では更新を利用不可にします。必要な安全条件を満たせない場合の利用不可は、計画上の継続目標と分けて表示する運用状態です。</span><span lang="en">Absent or unqualified automatic Failover is recorded as a limitation of the selected deployment. Mutations are unavailable where valid authority or required data cannot be established. Unavailability caused by unmet safety conditions is an observed operating state, recorded separately from the intended continuity target.</span>

# Security Relationship｜セキュリティとの関係

<span lang="ja">実行環境にだけ存在する変更や状態は、その環境の交換で引き継がれない場合があります。信頼できる成果物と構成から新しい環境を生成し、定期的に交換する運用は、同じ実行環境にその状態が残る期間を管理する手段になります。通常運転時の交換とセキュリティ対応時の交換には、環境生成、準備確認、受付変更などの共通部分があります。交換を繰り返した記録は、その経路を確認するための運用上の資料です。</span><span lang="en">Changes or state existing only in a runtime environment may be discarded when that environment is replaced. Construction from trusted artifacts and configuration, combined with scheduled replacement, provides a means to manage how long such state remains in the same runtime. Ordinary and security-triggered replacement share environment construction, readiness and admission-transfer mechanisms. Records of repeated replacement provide operational evidence about that path.</span>

<span lang="ja">実行環境を交換しても、盗まれた資格情報、流出した情報、不正に更新された永続データ、成果物自体の欠陥は別に残ります。対応には権限の失効、隔離、原因修正および永続状態の点検が必要です。侵害が疑われる旧環境は、通常の切戻し候補から除外します。環境交換は、認証・認可・監査などの対策を代替する機能ではありません。</span><span lang="en">Stolen credentials, disclosed information, maliciously modified persistent data and defects in artifacts require separate treatment after runtime replacement. Response includes revocation, isolation, cause correction and inspection of persistent state. A suspected compromised environment is excluded from ordinary switch-back candidates. Environment replacement does not substitute for authentication, authorization or audit controls.</span>

<span lang="ja">認証・認可・監査・区画分離を含む防御全体は、[[../../security/textus-cncf-security-architecture.dox/index.dox][Security技術ガイド]]を参照します。本書は環境交換に関係する性質と運用条件を扱います。HAの権限制御、同期および切替えプロトコルの詳細は、[[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][可用性・HA技術ガイド]]に分けています。</span><span lang="en">The [[../../security/textus-cncf-security-architecture.dox/index.dox][Security guide]] covers authentication, authorization, audit, containment and the wider defense model. This guide covers properties and operating conditions associated with environment replacement. The [[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][Availability and HA guide]] covers authority, synchronization and transfer protocols in detail.</span>

# Configuration, Quality Targets and Cost｜構成・品質目標・費用

<span lang="ja">運用設定は、可用性、復旧時間、データ保全、応答性、セキュリティおよび運用負担の要求に対応付けます。運用プロファイルは、その条件を設定としてまとめる設計です。要求した目標、選択した設定、採用版で利用できる機能および実際の確認結果を、それぞれ記録します。設定値だけを達成水準の根拠にはしません。</span><span lang="en">Operating settings are related to availability, recovery time, data preservation, responsiveness, security and operational-effort requirements. The profile design groups those conditions into configuration. Requirements, selected settings, capabilities available in the selected version and observed results are recorded separately. Configuration values alone are not evidence of an achieved service level.</span>

<span lang="ja">構成と運用条件のトレードオフ</span><span lang="en">Configuration and Operating Tradeoffs</span>

| <span lang="ja">選択</span><span lang="en">Choice</span> | <span lang="ja">効果と費用</span><span lang="en">Effect and Cost</span> |
| --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">単一環境の停止・再構築</span><span lang="en">Stop/reconstruct one environment</span> | <span lang="ja">資源費用を抑えやすいが交換中の停止を許容する必要がある</span><span lang="en">Lower resource demand, with downtime during replacement</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Primary＋準備済みRead Replica</span><span lang="en">Primary plus prepared Read Replica</span> | <span lang="ja">計画交換の継続性と参照分散を支えるが常時資源が増える</span><span lang="en">Supports planned continuity and read distribution at added steady resource cost</span> |
| <span lang="ja">旧環境の保持を長くする</span><span lang="en">Longer fallback retention</span> | <span lang="ja">観測・切戻しの機会が増える一方、資源・同期・互換性維持の費用が増える</span><span lang="en">More observation/fallback opportunity, with more resources, synchronization and compatibility costs</span> |
| <span lang="ja">短い交換間隔</span><span lang="en">Shorter replacement interval</span> | <span lang="ja">同じ実行環境の寿命を短くする一方、構築・同期・観測の頻度が増える</span><span lang="en">Shorter runtime lifetimes, with more frequent construction, synchronization and observation</span> |
| <span lang="ja">別ホストへの配置</span><span lang="en">Separate-host placement</span> | <span lang="ja">ホスト障害への対応には独立した配置・調停・保存経路の確認と費用が必要</span><span lang="en">Host-failure protection requires qualified independent placement, coordination and storage, with added cost</span> |

<span lang="ja">観測対象は、交換理由と対象版、受付主体、各環境の準備状態、同期遅延、完了待ち処理、保持期間、退役できない理由および直近の交換結果です。同一ホスト上の複数プロセスでの確認と、ホスト全体の停止に対する確認は異なります。要求した障害範囲と実際に確認した範囲を対応付けて記録します。</span><span lang="en">Observations include replacement reason/version, admission owner, environment readiness, synchronization lag, draining work, retention period, unmet retirement conditions and recent replacement outcomes. Qualification using several processes on one host differs from qualification against loss of that host. Records relate the requested failure boundary to the boundary actually exercised.</span>

# Implementation Plan and Qualification Status｜実装計画と検証状況

<span lang="ja">2026年11月13日時点のCNCF Phase 108は計画段階で、IR-01〜IR-05はOPENです。先行対象は計画交換です。受付・永続化・権限の接続、汎用キャッシュ同期、A・B・Cの交代、保持・反復運用、および実際の別実行環境と正本を用いた確認が開発項目になっています。自動障害切替えや広い配備構成は、この計画登録をもって実装済みとは扱いません。</span><span lang="en">As of 2026-11-13, CNCF Phase 108 is planned and IR-01 through IR-05 are OPEN. Planned replacement is the initial delivery scope. Development items cover admission/persistence/authority integration, shared cache synchronization, A/B/C transfer, retention/repeated operation and qualification using actual separate runtimes and authoritative data. Registration of these items does not establish delivered automatic Failover or broader deployment support.</span>

<span lang="ja">開発計画上の確認項目には、更新中のAからBへの受付移行、Aの確定結果の永続記録とB・Cへの反映、常駐状態喪失後の再構築、通知前クラッシュ後の追随、未準備環境の拒否、結果不明の照合および退役条件の適用があります。これらは検証予定の項目です。メモリ上の値やモックのみの確認では、実際の保存経路でのデータ保全は確認できません。</span><span lang="en">Planned qualification covers admission transfer from A to B during an update, persistence and B/C propagation of A commits, reconstruction after resident-state loss, catch-up after a crash before notification, refusal of unready environments, reconciliation of uncertain outcomes and enforcement of retirement conditions. These are planned checks. Memory-only values or mocks do not qualify preservation through the actual storage path.</span>

<span lang="ja">BoKとプロジェクトの知識は、採用理由、前提、品質目標、構成選択および検証結果の参照元です。実装・運用で得た結果は、レビューを経て後続の構成選択やAI駆動開発で参照する情報になります。知識に記載された方針と、採用版で確認された挙動は別に記録します。</span><span lang="en">The BoK and project knowledge provide references for rationale, assumptions, quality targets, configuration choices and qualification results. Reviewed implementation/operation findings inform subsequent configuration choices and AI-driven development. Documented policy and observed behavior in a selected version are recorded separately.</span>

# Related Documents and Design Sources｜関連資料と設計の参照元

<span lang="ja">[[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][可用性・HA技術ガイド]]は、サービス継続の目的、構成、同期、権限制御および切替えプロトコルを説明します。[[../../security/textus-cncf-security-architecture.dox/index.dox][Security技術ガイド]]は、防御全体での位置付けを扱います。[[../../reactive/textus-cncf-reactive-architecture.dox/index.dox][リアクティブ技術ガイド]]は、メモリ常駐、UnitOfWorkおよび回復可能性の関係を扱います。</span><span lang="en">The [[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][Availability and HA guide]] explains continuity objectives, architecture, synchronization, authority and transfer protocols. The [[../../security/textus-cncf-security-architecture.dox/index.dox][Security guide]] describes the wider defense context. The [[../../reactive/textus-cncf-reactive-architecture.dox/index.dox][Reactive guide]] covers memory residency, UnitOfWork and recoverability.</span>

<span lang="ja">Textus固有の設計根拠は、CNCFのAvailability Architecture、Subsystem Runtime ArchitectureおよびRuntime Cache Synchronizationです。実装計画はCNCF Phase 108が管理します。本書は、それらの設計と計画を説明する技術文書です。原典と更新日を参照し、実装契約と検証結果はCNCF側の記録で確認します。</span><span lang="en">Textus-specific design sources are CNCF Availability Architecture, Subsystem Runtime Architecture and Runtime Cache Synchronization. CNCF Phase 108 owns the implementation plan. This guide explains those designs and plans. Source documents and their revision dates identify the authority; CNCF records own implementation contracts and qualification results.</span>

<span lang="ja">一般的な背景資料として、Kief Morrisの「Immutable Server」（https://martinfowler.com/bliki/ImmutableServer.html）は、イミュータブルな環境とCI/CDの共通性、および保持するデータの扱いを説明しています。Chad Fowlerの「Trash Your Servers and Burn Your Code」（https://chadfowler.com/articles/trash-your-servers-and-burn-your-code.html）は、配備方式がアプリケーションコードの考え方にも影響したという経験を記述しています。Twelve-Factor AppのProcesses（https://12factor.net/processes）とDisposability（https://12factor.net/disposability）は、永続状態の分離、起動・終了、および中断時の処理条件を扱っています。これらは設計上の整理の参照元であり、CNCFの実装済み範囲を示す資料ではありません。</span><span lang="en">For general background, Kief Morris's Immutable Server (https://martinfowler.com/bliki/ImmutableServer.html) discusses parallels with CI/CD and handling of retained data. Chad Fowler's Trash Your Servers and Burn Your Code (https://chadfowler.com/articles/trash-your-servers-and-burn-your-code.html) reports how deployment choices affected his thinking about application code. The Twelve-Factor App chapters Processes (https://12factor.net/processes) and Disposability (https://12factor.net/disposability) address separation of durable state, startup/shutdown and interrupted-work conditions. These sources inform the design synthesis; they do not establish CNCF implementation status.</span>
